.TH DIPISDS 1 "2026-10-19" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipisds \- announce or discover DVB-IPI services via DVBSTP/SD&S

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdipisds\f1 \-a \-i \fIpath\f1 \-m \fImcast:port\f1 [\fIoptions\f1]
.br
\fBdipisds\f1 \-l \-m \fImcast:port\f1 [\fIoptions\f1]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdipisds\f1 implements DVBSTP-carried SD&S service discovery per ETSI TS 102 034 clause 5.
It runs in one of two mutually exclusive modes, selected by \fB\-a\f1 (announce, headend/injector role) or
\fB\-l\f1 (listen, client/receiver role).

.PP
\fB\-I\f1 selects the network interface used for the multicast join or send.
.br
\fB\-v\f1 prints periodic statistics to stderr: one line per announce cycle in \fB\-a\f1, one line per segment
received in \fB\-l\f1.
.br
\fB\-d\f1 daemonizes.

.SS Announce mode
.PP
In announce mode \fBdipisds\f1 reads a service list from \fB\-i\f1 and repeatedly transmits it as SD&S records
over DVBSTP on the multicast \fIgroup:port\f1 given by \fB\-m\f1, at the interval set by \fB\-t\f1.
Default: 5 seconds, ETSI TS 102 034 caps the full announce cycle at 30 seconds.
.PP
The input format is inferred from the \fB\-i\f1 suffix:

\fB.csv\f1 and \fB.m3u\f1 / \fB.m3u8\f1 use the same shapes as \fIdipiscan (1)\f1's output,
\fB.xspf\f1 is XSPF with the DVB triplet carried in a dvbipitools extension element,
and \fB.xml\f1 is a hand-authored or dipiscan-generated raw SD&S document that is sent
through unparsed.

For the structured formats, each entry's URI is \fBrtp:// [ @ ] addr : port\f1 or \fBudp:// [ @ ] addr : port\f1.
A missing TSId/OrigNetId defaults to 1, a missing ServiceId auto-increments from 1.
Duplicate OrigNetId/TSId/ServiceId triplets and inputs without services are errors.
CSV files (\fB\-i\f1, \fB\-\-packages\f1, \fB\-\-cells\f1) take RFC 4180 quoting, blanks around
fields are trimmed, a UTF-8 BOM is skipped, and lines starting with # are comments.
For the structured (non-.xml) inputs, \fB\-p\f1 and \fB\-O\f1 set the announced DomainName and provider display name,
and \fBdipisds\f1 additionally synthesizes a Service Provider Discovery record pointing back
at the same multicast socket.

A set of \fB\-\-ret\-\f1, \fB\-\-fcc\-\f1, \fB\-\-packages\f1, \fB\-\-cells\f1, \fB\-\-rms\-\f1, \fB\-\-fus\-\f1, and \fB\-\-bcg\-\f1
options extend the announced Broadcast Discovery and RMS-FUS records for dipifccret RET/FCC retransmission servers,
Package Discovery, Regionalisation Discovery, RMS-FUS Discovery, and BCG Discovery. These options are announce-only and, with
the exception of the metrics options, have no effect on raw \fB.xml\f1 input.
.PP
\fISIGHUP\f1 re-reads \fB\-i\f1. On a parse error the previous input keeps being announced.
Each generated document has its own segment version, bumped (modulo 256) only when that
document changed.
For raw \fB.xml\f1 input the segment version is the Version attribute of the record element
(ServiceProvider for Service Provider Discovery), so it stays unchanged when the document does.
Without the attribute it is bumped when the content changed.

.SS Listen mode
.PP
In listen mode \fBdipisds\f1 joins the multicast group at \fB\-m\f1, reassembles DVBSTP segments, and after
\fB\-t\f1 seconds (default: 35) writes whatever Broadcast Discovery records it saw as a playlist to
\fB\-o\f1 (default stdout). The output format is selected by \fB\-f\f1 or inferred from the \fB\-o\f1 suffix.
\fBxml\f1 dumps each reassembled SD&S document as received, one after another with its own XML declaration,
so output from more than one segment is not a single well-formed XML file. \fBnull\f1 discards the output.
.PP
Segments with compression 001 are BiM-encoded SD&S (TS 102 034 5.5.2) and are decoded to XML first.
Supported namespaces: urn:dvb:metadata:iptv:sdns:2014-1, 2012-1, 2008-1 and urn:dvb:ipi:sdns:2006.
\fB\-\-bim\-namespace\f1 (config \fBbim-namespace\f1) fixes the namespace, otherwise the newest one decoding the segment
exactly wins. Without zlib such segments are dropped.
.PP
\fB\-s\f1 (config \fBschema\f1, a list) decodes them through an XSD instead of the compiled-in schemas: one schema file, or directories
searched for the schema of \fB\-\-bim\-namespace\f1. Without it the namespace of the schema file is used.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS Mode selection
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-announce
Headend mode: read
.BR \-i ,
transmit on
.BR \-m .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen
Client mode: receive on
.BR \-m ,
write
.BR \-o .
.SS Common options
.TP
.BI \-m " group" : port
.RB ( \-\-mcast )
Multicast group:port. Use
.RI [ addr6 ]: port
for IPv6. Required in both modes.
.TP
.BI \-I " iface"
.RB ( \-\-iface )
Multicast interface.
.TP
.BI \-\-dscp " v"
Announce: output DSCP marking (ETSI TS 102 034 Table 29):
.RI ( video-high | video-low | voice | signalling | best-effort ,
or a raw DSCP value 0..63, default
.BR signalling ).
.TP
.BI \-T " n"
.RB ( \-\-ttl )
Announce: multicast TTL (IPv4) or hop limit (IPv6), 1..255, default 16.
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds"
Announce mode
.RB ( \-\-interval ):
repeat interval, default 5. Listen mode
.RB ( \-\-timeout ):
stop after N seconds, default 35;
.B 0
listens until SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic stats on stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " when"
.RI ( auto | always | never ,
default
.BR auto ).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config\ \fI<path>\fR
YAML configuration file. Keys mirror the options above. Without this option,
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipisds.yaml
is read if it exists.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-strict
Treat configuration file issues (unknown or duplicate keys, invalid values,
conflicting settings, unreadable referenced files) as errors instead of
warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-configtest
Check the configuration file (from
.B \-c
or the default location) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SS Announce mode options (\-a)
.TP
.BI \-i " path"
.RB ( \-\-input )
A
.BR .csv / .m3u / .xspf
playlist or raw SD&S
.B .xml
document.
.TP
.BI \-p " name"
.RB ( \-\-provider )
DomainName. Required unless
.B \-i
is
.BR .xml .
.TP
.BI \-O " name"
.RB ( \-\-offering )
Display name. Required unless
.B \-i
is
.BR .xml .
.TP
.BI \-L " code"
.RB ( \-\-lang )
ISO 639-2 code for the display name (default
.BR deu ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-addr " addr" : port
Advertise a
.BR dipifccret (1)
RET server (its
.B \-l
value). Opt-in; adds RTPRetransmission to every announced service.
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-rtx\-time " ms"
RET rtx-time, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-B
(default 2000).
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-rtx\-pt " n"
RET RTP payload type, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-R
(default 99).
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-mc
Also advertise multicast RET (as
.BR dipifccret (1)
does without
.BR \-\-no\-mc\-ret ).
Group:port always match the service's own IPMulticastAddress, per Annex
F.6.2.2's same-group:port reuse.
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-mc\-port " port"
Multicast RET port, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-F .
Default: each service's own port.
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-rsi\-mc\-ret
RSI (Annex F.5.3) rides the multicast RET session instead of the default
session. Requires
.BR \-\-ret\-mc ;
matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-\-rsi\-mc\-ret .
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-addr " addr" : port
Advertise a
.BR dipifccret (1)
FCC server (its
.B \-l
value). Opt-in; adds ServerBasedEnhancementServiceInfo to every announced
service. Separate element from
.BR \-\-ret\-addr 's
RTPRetransmission; both can be given together, but per Annex I.2.3 an HNED
using both services is meant to prefer this element.
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-rtx\-time " ms"
FCC Retransmission_session rtx-time (default 2000).
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-rtx\-pt " n"
FCC RTP payload type, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-R
(default 99).
.TP
.B \-\-fcc\-resolve\-by\-port
Per-service FCC port instead of
.BR \-\-fcc\-addr 's
port. Matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-\-fcc\-resolve\-by\-port .
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-resolve\-base\-port " port"
Matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-\-fcc\-resolve\-base\-port .
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-resolve\-max\-channels " n"
Port hash modulus for resolve-by-port (default 300).
.TP
.BI \-\-al\-fec\-addr " addr" : port
Advertises an Annex E Layer 1 FEC (SMPTE 2022-1) repair stream: adds a
.B FECBaseLayer
element to every service's
.BR IPMulticastAddress .
Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-al\-fec\-pt " n"
FEC repair stream RTP payload type (default 96). Requires
.BR \-\-al\-fec\-addr .
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics " path"
Unix datagram socket for metrics (default
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock ).
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-id " name"
Stable instance id. Metrics are disabled unless this is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-interval " seconds"
Snapshot interval (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-packages " path"
Package Discovery (payload 0x05) from
.I id,name,lang,visible,svc1|svc2|...
lines.
.I id
is the numeric Id;
.I name
/
.I lang
set PackageName and its ISO 639-2 language;
.I visible
is 0 or 1 (default 1). Each service name must match exactly one
.B \-i
entry by ServiceName, whose DVBTriplet is added.
.TP
.BI \-\-cells " path"
Regionalisation Discovery (payload 0x07) from
.I id,country,type:value,...
lines.
.I id
is the Cell's Id, matched against ServiceAvailability/PackageAvailability
Cells elsewhere;
.I country
is the 2-letter ISO 3166 CountryCode. The
.I type:value
pairs are RFC 4676 civic address types, nested outer to inner in the given
order: a single chain per cell, not a branching CA tree.
.TP
.BI \-\-bim\-namespace " ns"
Listen: BiM SD&S namespace (urn:dvb:metadata:iptv:sdns:2014-1, 2012-1, 2008-1,
urn:dvb:ipi:sdns:2006). Default: the newest that decodes the segment exactly.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-schema " \fIpath\fR"
Listen: SD&S schema file, or directory searched for the schema of \fB\-\-bim\-namespace\fR, decoding BiM segments
through it. Repeatable, one schema file at most. Default: the compiled-in schemas.
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-name " name"
RMS Discovery display name. Requires
.BR \-\-rms\-location .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-fus\-name :
RMSFUSDiscovery carries one provider type or the other, never both.
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-lang " code"
ISO 639-2 code for
.B \-\-rms\-name
(default
.BR deu ).
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-location " uri"
RMSType RMSLocation.
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-logo " uri"
RMSType LogoURI.
.TP
.BI \-\-bcg\-name " name"
BCG Discovery record (payload 6, TS 102 034 5.2.13.1) with this name. Requires
.BR \-\-bcg\-mcast .
.TP
.BI \-\-bcg\-id " id"
BCG id, referenced from the Broadcast Discovery records. Requires
.BR \-\-bcg\-name .
.TP
.BI \-\-bcg\-description " text"
BCG description. Requires
.BR \-\-bcg\-name .
.TP
.BI \-\-bcg\-provider\-name " name"
BCG provider name. Requires
.BR \-\-bcg\-name .
.TP
.BI \-\-bcg\-mcast " addr" : port
Multicast location of the BCG (e.g. the
.B dipibcg \-m
group).
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-name " name"
FUS Discovery display name. Requires
.BR \-\-fus\-id .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-rms\-name .
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-lang " code"
ISO 639-2 code for
.B \-\-fus\-name
(default
.BR deu ).
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-id " n"
FUSID (decimal).
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-announce " addr" : port
FUS MulticastAnnouncementAddress.
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-logo " uri"
FUSType LogoURI.
.SS Listen mode options (\-l)
.TP
.BI \-o " path"
.RB ( \-\-output )
Output path,
.B \-
for stdout (default).
.TP
.BI \-f " fmt"
.RB ( \-\-format )
.RI ( m3u | csv | xspf | xml | null ,
default taken from the
.B \-o
suffix (.csv, .xspf, .xml), else m3u).

.SH SCOPE
DVBSTP framing is generic
on announce, the structured (non-.xml) side understands Service Provider Discovery, Broadcast Discovery, Package
Discovery, Regionalisation Discovery, and RMS-FUS Discovery (payloads
0x01/0x02/0x05/0x07/0x08), each a minimal producer subset of its ETSI TS 102 034 clause 5.2.13 type.
Anything wider goes through \fB.xml\f1 passthrough. Listen (\fB\-l\f1) is Broadcast Discovery only.
.PP
Not a general SD&S client: CoD and BCG-carriage records (\fBdipibcg\f1 (1) covers BCG) are not supported here.
Compression is always none: gzip is spec-restricted to other payload ids, BiM is not implemented.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipisds \-a \-i channels.csv \-p example.org \-O "My Headend" \-m 239.255.0.1:3937
Announce a CSV playlist as an SD&S service list.
.TP
.B dipisds \-l \-m 239.255.0.1:3937 \-o discovered.m3u
Listen for the announcement and write the discovered services as an m3u playlist.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipisds.yaml
Default configuration file, read if present. An example with all defaults ships as
.IR /usr/share/dvbipitools/etc/dipisds.yaml .

